#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087441 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "4f4be86f-5a12-5fdf-b98e-2095b1faae8f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4499" :question/problem "Using the method of direct verification, determine whether the matrix $B$ is the inverse of $A,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We must check whether $AB = BA = I_2.$\n\nComputing $AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087442 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "7ab2814b-dc93-569b-bdd6-618880da6e2c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4500" :question/problem "Using the method of direct verification, determine whether the matrix $B$ is the inverse of $A,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we  check whether $AB = BA = I_3.$\n\nComputing $AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c298b7c0-87d8-5070-9326-e5f72ddfb342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302799} {:answer/id #uuid "68ddd868-516f-51ed-b28e-17e881310145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302800} {:answer/id #uuid "19e63d16-9b79-5c82-887f-d529fe29d764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302801} {:answer/id #uuid "927af9a2-2efa-5578-8c28-0f9e1016e485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302802} {:answer/id #uuid "850949f9-ad9a-5be9-a51e-9d461406a620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "850949f9-ad9a-5be9-a51e-9d461406a620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302803} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a87424d-e6bf-5c52-9c4b-54d345cccfc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6a07c18-bf7c-5e80-8309-27a2f04c7f2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102669" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- $B={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "667351d6-2ba5-58b0-bcbe-7e7ab450f2a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302806} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec94cc3-d5aa-50a6-871f-1867f5821654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302807} {:answer/id #uuid "d5be058a-dcf7-543d-8bfc-c912c4149f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302808} {:answer/id #uuid "60d9d2ad-3940-5bec-b88a-a2481126e5cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302809} {:answer/id #uuid "640a2fd0-1a8e-5656-899a-ed2bc26968da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "667351d6-2ba5-58b0-bcbe-7e7ab450f2a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302806} :answer-field/id #uuid "b428c409-1390-5741-9418-c8be3619edb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c47df1f8-b875-59be-a742-b863c4a0e655" :question/math-academy-id "q-102673" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- $C={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $C={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77c867c4-8757-5470-b7a4-85e405eb831e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302813} {:answer/id #uuid "a3374b96-d59e-500d-a5cd-56e1e6dfbe0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302814} {:answer/id #uuid "29ddaa95-aefa-5c4e-9d21-5d3a22240a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302815} {:answer/id #uuid "e236ee0f-0944-510a-87e0-e5e688e61385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302816} {:answer/id #uuid "931c5976-7b9c-5379-9db4-0b022d013be0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "931c5976-7b9c-5379-9db4-0b022d013be0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302817} :answer-field/id #uuid "4408eafe-0193-5010-acbd-7591641b4d0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ee7649a-0e9f-5e8e-9cba-9546fd564117" :question/math-academy-id "q-11634" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,C=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n- $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- $B={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. \nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81f8be80-9139-5e1a-83ff-995c328f3cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276999} {:answer/id #uuid "8f4dc48e-a57f-5e2a-85c8-763e60a37661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277000} {:answer/id #uuid "a4343b4d-1d2a-57e4-8f1d-759cee6e14a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277001} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a6ec6c-03b0-5cbb-b694-43b91ca265ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277002} {:answer/id #uuid "0a58a9d4-2524-5f94-a07c-7b06fefeba35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81f8be80-9139-5e1a-83ff-995c328f3cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276999} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3fe6216-d9f1-5132-9fe1-6eeefed6e416" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c50f86c-ddb1-5c05-8a97-ab13cd9bdcec" :question/math-academy-id "q-11637" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $CD=DC={I}_{2}$\n- $DE=ED={I}_{2}$\n- $D={C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "800ac08d-0264-581f-a3ee-3390c3fdb0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084568} {:answer/id #uuid "f89c57e7-272d-5d16-92e1-da9cba13d1c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084569} {:answer/id #uuid "1d2af7e5-377a-54b6-a0fc-e57aa70b6ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084570} {:answer/id #uuid "345f02a1-7bff-5d02-ba54-96d7361ba6be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084571} {:answer/id #uuid "3519042d-ca9e-5050-b961-a6106adb9e5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f89c57e7-272d-5d16-92e1-da9cba13d1c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084569} :answer-field/id #uuid "63a8abe3-2631-56cf-8548-e8b2d74e9890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1ac1576-214f-54b1-9885-54ce227fd5fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-11642" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $CD=DC={I}_{3}$\n- $CE=EC={I}_{3}$\n- $E={C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{3}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $CE=EC={I}_{3}.$ Computing $CE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CE & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $E\\ne {C}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/ans